      "markdown": "The Lavery, Cromwell Place, South Kensington\n\n# Calico Wallpaper x BEVERLY 1975: Cadence at The Lavery, Brompton Design District\n\nA feature wall of Calico's Cadence, in Oxblood, hung in a single day on site for New York homewares shop BEVERLY 1975's first London presentation, at The Lavery.\n\n![Cadence Oxblood behind BEVERLY 1975's tables during Brompton Design District.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-08-800.webp)\n\n## Project record\n\nClient, materials & project facts\n\n**Client**\n: Calico Wallpaper (Brooklyn, New York), for BEVERLY 1975 CONCIERGE\n\n**Designer**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Main contractor**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Maker and paper**\n: Calico Wallpaper – Cadence by Athena Calderone, Oxblood\n\n**Area or rooms**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Scope**\n: Wallcovering installation (feature wall)\n\n**Year**\n: 2026\n\n**Delivered in partnership with [Calico Wallpaper](https://calicowallpaper.com/).**\n\n**In the press:** [Family Style, BEVERLY 1975 at Brompton Design District](https://www.family.style/articles/beverly-1975-brompton-design-district-london) · [Martyn White, “BEVERLY 1975 CONCIERGE: Beverly Nguyen Comes to London”](https://martynwhite.co/beverly-1975-concierge-beverly-nguyen-brompton/) · [The Design Release, CONCIERGE event listing](https://www.thedesignrelease.com/event/lon-the-lavery-concierge) · [Calico Wallpaper on LinkedIn, opening night (12 Sep 2026)](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/calico-wallpaper_last-night-we-celebrated-the-opening-of-activity-7504542081961586688-GePL)\n\n## At a glance\n\n- **In partnership with:** Calico Wallpaper, Brooklyn\n- **Exhibitor:** BEVERLY 1975 (Beverly Nguyen), launching CONCIERGE, its travelling retail concept\n- **Event:** Brompton Design District, London Design Festival 2026, 12–20 September\n- **Venue:** The Lavery, Cromwell Place, South Kensington\n- **Installed:** 8 September 2026, one day on site\n- **Product:** Cadence by Athena Calderone, in Oxblood\n\n## The project\n\nFor its first London appearance, BEVERLY 1975 built its space around its signature pegboard. Behind it ran Calico Wallpaper’s Cadence, designed with Athena Calderone. In Oxblood it reads, in one reviewer’s words, “as aged patina”: a deep, layered red that sets off ceramics, textiles and lighting.\n\n## Our approach\n\n- **Prepared for a perfect finish.** Cadence’s quiet, layered texture shows every imperfection in the wall beneath, so preparation came first.\n- **Seams that disappear.** With a tonal, painterly ground there is no motif to hide a join in. Every seam was butted and rolled to vanish.\n- **One day, ready for styling.** The wall was finished in a single day, leaving the space clear for the BEVERLY team to style before the opening.\n\n## Links and press\n\n- [Cadence collection (Alabaster, Fawn, Jasper, Oxblood, Porcelain)](https://calicowallpaper.com/collection/cadence/)\n- [Family Style, BEVERLY 1975 at Brompton Design District](https://www.family.style/articles/beverly-1975-brompton-design-district-london)\n- [Martyn White, “BEVERLY 1975 CONCIERGE: Beverly Nguyen Comes to London”](https://martynwhite.co/beverly-1975-concierge-beverly-nguyen-brompton/)\n- [The Design Release, CONCIERGE event listing](https://www.thedesignrelease.com/event/lon-the-lavery-concierge)\n- [Calico Wallpaper on LinkedIn, opening night (12 Sep 2026)](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/calico-wallpaper_last-night-we-celebrated-the-opening-of-activity-7504542081961586688-GePL)\n\n## Photographs\n\n![The finished Cadence Oxblood feature wall at The Lavery, Cromwell Place.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-06-800.webp)\n\n![Close-up of the layered texture of Cadence in Oxblood.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-07-800.webp)\n\n![Seam detail in Cadence Oxblood.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-05-800.webp)\n\n![Calico Wallpaper Cadence in Oxblood going up on the feature wall.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-04-800.webp)\n\n![Preparing the wall at The Lavery, Cromwell Place, before hanging.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-03-800.webp)\n\nHow the commission ran\n\n## The same standards, on every commission.\n\nEach commission has a written scope by room, walls prepared until they are true, protected floors, batch and shade control, set-out from the room’s focal points, and a return visit. [Read the method](https://www.mrwallcover.com/practice/#method).\n\nThe six standards in full\n\n01\n\n### Survey and scope, room by room\n\nWe measure the wall that will actually be hung, allow for the repeat and the wastage, and write a scope of works room by room before anyone orders paper.\n\n02\n\n### Preparation decides the finish\n\nWalls are filled, made good and primed until they are true. If a wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\n03\n\n### Protection and containment\n\nFloors, furniture and finished joinery are protected as part of the hang. Work is contained and the place is left tidy each evening. In a home we are visitors; in a hotel we work around the house.\n\n04\n\n### Batch and shade control\n\nDeliveries are checked against the measure, and batches and shading are managed so that a corridor of rooms reads as one surface.\n\n05\n\n### Set out from the room's focal points\n\nPattern is set out from chimneypieces, doorcases and bed walls, so the pattern sits square to the cornice and the joinery.\n\n06\n\n### One team, then the return visit\n\nThe people who start are the people who finish. Four to six weeks after completion we come back to look at every seam and edge, and the workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months.\n\n[See the finish up close: seams, internal corners, edges and joins from our own installations](https://www.mrwallcover.com/details/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 22 October 2026\n",
